.TH PRISM-CTL 1 "2026-11-22" "Prism" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prism-ctl \- control the Prism desktop shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prism-ctl
.I target
.RI [ action ]
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B prism-ctl
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prism-ctl
sends one command to
.BR prismd ,
the Prism daemon, over its socket
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/prism.sock ,
and prints the answer.
It is meant for compositor keybinds and scripts: every overlay, card and
setting that has a keybind in Prism is reached through it.
.PP
Most targets that open a card take
.BR toggle ,
.B open
and
.BR close ;
when the action is left out they toggle.
Targets that switch something on or off take
.B on
or
.B off
(also
.BR true / false ,
.BR 1 / 0 );
anything else, or nothing, toggles.
.PP
.B prismd
runs as the systemd user unit
.BR prismd.service ;
.B prism-ctl
does not start it.
.SH OVERLAYS AND CARDS
.TP
.B launcher \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The app launcher.
.TP
.BI "launcher query " text
Print the first 10 installed apps matching
.I text
and their desktop ids, without opening the launcher.
.TP
.B launcher list
Print the number of installed apps and the first 15.
.TP
.BI "launcher run " id
Launch the app whose desktop id is
.I id
(case does not matter), for example
.BR "prism-ctl launcher run firefox" .
.TP
.B search \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The search card (apps, files, quick answers).
.TP
.BI "search query " text
Open search with
.I text
typed in, replacing what it had.
.TP
.BI "search results " text
Print the apps and files matching
.IR text ,
without opening search.
.TP
.B settings \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The Settings card.
.TP
.BI "settings tab " tab
Open Settings on a tab, or switch the open card to it.
.I tab
is a name (case, spaces and hyphens do not matter, and a prefix that fits only
one tab is enough, for example
.BR lock\-screen ,
.B wall
or
.BR dis )
or a number from 1 to 18 in this order: Appearance, Wallpaper, Desktop,
Calendar, Bar, Dock, Launcher, Search, Notifications, Lock Screen, Greeter,
Power, Display, Connections, Phone, Capture, Downloads, System.
.TP
.B setup
The first-time setup guide.
.B guide
is a synonym.
.TP
.B deps \fR[\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
List the programs and services Prism uses that are missing on this computer, with what each is
for, how important it is (needed, recommended, optional) and its Arch Linux package, then the
.B pacman
command that installs them. Works without a running
.BR prismd ;
the installer runs it at the end. With
.BR \-\-quiet ,
prints nothing when everything is installed. Exits 1 when something needed is missing.
.TP
.B notes \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The Notes card.
.TP
.B clipboard \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The clipboard history card.
.TP
.B emoji \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The emoji picker.
.TP
.B keybinds \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBedit\fR|\fBrules\fR]
The keybind cheat sheet.
.B list
prints the binds,
.B edit
opens the Shortcuts editor and
.B rules
the Window Rules editor.
.TP
.B power \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The power menu.
.TP
.B notif \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The notification center.
.TP
.B phone \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The Phone card. See
.B PHONE
for the other phone commands.
.TP
.B wallpaper \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The wallpaper picker.
.TP
.B switcher \fR[\fBnext\fR|\fBprev\fR|\fBshow\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The window switcher. Bind
.B next
to Alt+Tab and
.B prev
to Alt+Shift+Tab; releasing Alt picks the selected window.
.B show
opens it without moving the selection. Default:
.BR next .
.TP
.B colorpicker \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBpick\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The colour picker. The picked colour is copied to the clipboard.
.TP
.B desktop \fR[\fBedit\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR|\fBsave\fR|\fBdiscard\fR|\fBreset\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
Desktop widget edit mode.
.B edit
toggles it,
.B save
and
.B discard
leave it keeping or dropping the changes,
.B reset
restores the default layout and
.B status
prints whether it is open.
.B edit-mode
is the same target without the
.B edit
action.
.SH SCREENSHOTS AND RECORDING
.B capture
is a synonym of
.BR screenshot .
.TP
.B screenshot \fR[\fBtoggle\fR]
Open or close the capture overlay.
.TP
.B screenshot region\fR|\fBwindow\fR|\fBtext
Open the overlay in that mode.
.B text
(also
.BR ocr )
copies the text in the chosen region; it needs
.BR tesseract (1).
.TP
.BI "screenshot open " mode
Open the overlay in
.I mode
.RB ( region ,
.BR window ,
.BR text ).
.TP
.B screenshot screen \fR[\fB\-\-no\-save\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-clipboard\fR]
Take the whole screen at once, without the overlay. It is saved and copied
unless told otherwise.
.B output
is a synonym.
.TP
.B screenshot close
Close the overlay.
.TP
.B screenshot record
Stop the running recording, or open the overlay in record mode.
.TP
.B screenshot stop
Stop the running recording.
.TP
.B screenshot status
Print the recording state as JSON.
.TP
.B screenshot replay \fR[\fBsave\fR|\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBtoggle\fR]
The replay buffer.
.B save
(the default) writes the last seconds to a file;
.BR on ,
.B off
and
.B toggle
switch the buffer.
.SH MEDIA, VOLUME AND BRIGHTNESS
.TP
.B media \fR[\fBstatus\fR|\fBplay\-pause\fR|\fBnext\fR|\fBprev\fR|\fBstop\fR]
Control the current MPRIS player.
.B status
(the default) prints what is playing.
.BR play ,
.B pause
and
.B toggle
are synonyms of
.BR play\-pause ;
.B previous
of
.BR prev .
.TP
.B osd volume \fR[\fB+\fIstep\fB%\fR|\fB\-\fIstep\fB%\fR|\fBmute\fR|\fIvalue\fR]
Change the output volume by
.I step
percent, set it to
.I value
percent, or toggle mute, and show the OSD. A step without a number is 5.
.TP
.B osd brightness \fR[\fB+\fIstep\fB%\fR|\fB\-\fIstep\fB%\fR|\fIvalue\fR]
The same for screen brightness.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
.TP
.B notif list
Print the stored notifications.
.TP
.B notif clear
Remove all notifications.
.TP
.BI "notif dismiss " id
Remove one notification.
.TP
.B notif send \fR[\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-app \fIname\fR] [\fIsummary\fR [\fIbody\fR]]
Post a notification. With three words and no
.BR \-a ,
the first is the app name.
.TP
.B notif silent \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR]
Do not disturb: notifications are stored without popups.
.TP
.B notif state
Print silent mode, caffeinate, game mode and the timer as JSON.
.SH TIMER
.TP
.BI "timer start " duration
Start a timer.
.I duration
is like
.BR 5m ,
.BR 90s ,
.B 1h30m
or
.BR 2:30 .
.B prism-ctl timer
.I duration
does the same.
.TP
.BI "timer add " duration
Add time to the running timer; a leading
.B \-
takes it away.
.TP
.B timer pause\fR|\fBresume\fR|\fBcancel
Pause, resume or cancel the timer.
.B stop
is a synonym of
.BR cancel .
.TP
.B timer \fR[\fBstatus\fR]
Print the timer and stopwatch state as JSON.
.TP
.B stopwatch \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBreset\fR]
Start or pause the stopwatch, or reset it.
.SH SYSTEM
.TP
.B lock \fR[\fBlock\fR]
Lock the session with
.BR prism-lock .
.TP
.B lock status
Print whether the session is locked and idle.
.TP
.B power lock\fR|\fBlogout\fR|\fBsuspend\fR|\fBsleep\fR|\fBhibernate\fR|\fBreboot\fR|\fBshutdown
Act at once, without the menu.
.B exit
is a synonym of
.BR logout ,
.B restart
of
.B reboot
and
.B poweroff
of
.BR shutdown .
.TP
.B caffeinate \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR]
Keep the screen awake (idle inhibitor).
.TP
.B gamemode \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR]
Game mode: silent notifications, the performance power profile, no
animations or blur. Turning it off restores the earlier state.
.B game\-mode
is a synonym.
.TP
.B calendar \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR]
The Calendar card: the month with its events and the selected day's agenda.
Without an action it toggles. A click on the bar's clock does the same.
.TP
.B calendar refresh
Read the calendars of online accounts (evolution-data-server) again now.
The event card sends it after adding, changing or deleting an event.
.TP
.B bluelight \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBmanual_toggle\fR|\fBdump\fR]
.B toggle
switches the blue light filter's schedule,
.B manual_toggle
turns the filter on or off now and
.B dump
prints its state as JSON.
.TP
.B network \fR[\fBstatus\fR|\fBtoggle\-wifi\fR]
Print the network state, or switch Wi-Fi.
.TP
.B bluetooth \fR[\fBstatus\fR|\fBtoggle\fR]
Print the Bluetooth state, or switch Bluetooth.
.SH THEME AND WALLPAPER
.TP
.BI "wallpaper set " path " \fR[\fIscheme\fR [\fImode\fR]]"
Set the wallpaper with the configured wallpaper daemon and regenerate the
colours with
.BR matugen .
.I scheme
is a matugen scheme type (for example
.BR scheme\-tonal\-spot )
and
.I mode
is
.B dark
or
.BR light .
.TP
.B wallpaper get
Print the current wallpaper's path.
.TP
.B theme \fR[\fBreload\fR]
Reload the colour palette.
.TP
.B theme palette
Print the palette as JSON.
.B get
is a synonym.
.TP
.B depth \fR[\fBstatus\fR|\fBgenerate\fR|\fBclear\fR]
The wallpaper depth mask (the clock drawn behind the foreground).
.B generate
makes it for the current wallpaper and
.B clear
deletes all cached masks.
.TP
.B index \fR[\fBstatus\fR|\fBrebuild\fR]
The file index used by search.
.SH DOWNLOADS
Prism's download manager. A download starts on one connection and adds more
while they help (up to the Connections per Download setting), and continues
after a pause or a restart when the server allows it. Files go to the Download
Folder setting (Settings, Downloads), are written as
.I name.prismdl
until complete, and a notification offers Open and Show in Folder when one is
done. The Prism Downloads Firefox extension uses the same commands.
.B downloads
is a synonym.
.TP
.B download toggle\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose
The Downloads card: the list with Pause, Resume, Cancel, Open, Show in Folder
and Remove, and a field to paste a link into. A click on the downloads pill
opens it too.
.TP
.B download \fR[\fBlist\fR]
Print every download with its id, state, size and speed.
.TP
.BI "download add " url " \fR[\fB\-\-name \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-dir \fIfolder\fR] [\fB\-\-referer \fIurl\fR] [\fB\-\-cookie \fIheader\fR] [\fB\-\-user\-agent \fIstring\fR] [\fB\-\-ask\fR] [\fB\-\-hls \fR[\fB\-\-variant \fIurl\fR]]"
Queue a download and print its id. With
.B \-\-ask
it waits in the confirmation card first (when Confirm Browser Downloads is on).
.B \-\-hls
(assumed for links ending in
.IR .m3u8 )
downloads an HLS video stream (AES-128 encrypted ones too; live streams and DRM
are refused) as one MP4, joined with
.BR ffmpeg (1);
.B \-\-variant
picks a quality from a master playlist (default: the best).
.B \-o
and
.B \-d
are short for
.B \-\-name
and
.BR \-\-dir .
.TP
.BI "download start " id " \fR[\fB\-\-name \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-dir \fIfolder\fR]"
Start a download that waits for confirmation (added with
.BR \-\-ask ,
as the Firefox extension does when Confirm Browser Downloads is on), optionally
under another name or in another folder. This is the confirmation card's
Download button.
.TP
.BI "download decline " id
Forget a download still waiting for confirmation (the card's Cancel).
.TP
.BI "download pause " id
.TQ
.BI "download resume " id
Pause, or continue a paused or failed download.
.B retry
is a synonym of
.BR resume .
.TP
.BI "download cancel " id
Stop and delete what was fetched; the entry stays as cancelled.
.TP
.BI "download remove " id
Forget an entry (cancelling it when it runs). A finished file stays.
.B rm
is a synonym.
.TP
.BI "download open " id
.TQ
.BI "download show " id
Open a finished download, or show it in the file manager.
.TP
.B download clear
Forget finished, failed and cancelled entries.
.SH CLIPBOARD AND EMOJI
.TP
.B clipboard list
Print the 10 latest entries with their index.
.TP
.BI "clipboard get " index
Print an entry.
.TP
.BI "clipboard copy " index
Copy an entry back to the clipboard.
.TP
.BI "clipboard add " text
Add text to the history.
.TP
.B clipboard clear
Clear the history.
.TP
.BI "emoji search " query
Print matching emoji.
.TP
.BI "emoji copy " glyph
Add an emoji to the clipboard history.
.TP
.B emoji list
Print the first 20 emoji with their names.
.SH PHONE
These need phone sync to be on in Settings
.RB ( prism\-phoned ).
Commands that take an optional
.I device
use the connected phone when it is left out.
.TP
.B phone status
Print the known devices and their state.
.TP
.B phone refresh
Look for devices again.
.TP
.BI "phone connect " ip\fR[\fB:\fIport\fR]
Connect to a phone by address.
.TP
.B phone pair\fR|\fBunpair\fR|\fBaccept\fR|\fBreject \fR[\fIdevice\fR]
Ask to pair, forget a pairing, or answer a pair request.
.TP
.B phone ping\fR|\fBring \fR[\fIdevice\fR]
Send a ping, or make the phone ring.
.TP
.BI "phone clipboard " text
Put
.I text
on the phone's clipboard.
.TP
.B phone media \fR[\fBplay\fR|\fBpause\fR|\fBnext\fR|\fBprevious\fR]
Control the phone's media player. Without an action it toggles play and
pause.
.TP
.BI "phone send " file ...
Send files.
.TP
.BI "phone send \-\-text " text
Send text.
.TP
.BI "phone send \-\-url " url
Open a link on the phone.
.SH OTHER
.TP
.B ping
Check that prismd answers.
.TP
.B help
Print prismd's greeting.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command line could not be parsed.
.TP
.B 2
prismd is not running (the socket could not be reached).
.TP
.BR 3 ", " 4 ", " 5
The command could not be sent or the answer read.
.TP
.B 6
prismd refused the command; the reason is printed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/prism.sock
prismd's command socket.
.TP
.I ~/.config/prism/config.json
Settings. Changed by Settings and by commands such as
.B gamemode
and
.BR "screenshot replay on" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/prism/notes.json
Notes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/prism/dock.json
Dock pins.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prism/downloads.json
The download list, with what is left of each download.
.SH EXAMPLES
Keybinds for MangoWM:
.PP
.RS
.nf
bind=SUPER,space,spawn,prism-ctl launcher
bind=ALT,Tab,spawn,prism-ctl switcher next
bind=NONE,XF86AudioRaiseVolume,spawn,prism-ctl osd volume +5%
bind=NONE,Print,spawn,prism-ctl screenshot region
.fi
.RE
.PP
A five-minute timer, and a notification when a script is done:
.PP
.RS
.nf
prism-ctl timer 5m
make && prism-ctl notif send -a make "Build finished"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR matugen (1)
.PP
Logs of prismd and prism-ui:
.B journalctl \-\-user \-u prismd
